 34SI cDNE$Evaluators take a weighted average when multiple measurements of a   
 34SI2cDN E(n){-lab} are available. 2019Wa38 reported the E(n){-lab} measured by
 34SI3cDN two neutron detectors. 2005Ti11 reported the E(level) of {+35}Si      
 34SI4cDN neutron-emitting levels. Evaluators deduced neutron center-of-mass    
 34SI5cDN energies E{-c.m.}=E(level)({+35}Si)-S(n)({+35}Si)-E(level)({+34}Si)   
 34SI6cDN using the original S(n)=2474 {I43} used by 2005Ti11. Evaluators then  
 34SI7cDN deduced each E(n){-lab}=E{-c.m.}|*m({+34}Si)/[m(n)+m({+34}Si)] for    
 34SI8cDN 2005Ti11.                                                             
